  Vulnerability: Modern calibration techniques (temperature scaling, conformal prediction, Bayesian deep learning, and retrieval-augmented systems) have made meaningful empirical progress on uncertainty quantification; a sophisticated critic could argue that OOD overconfidence is an engineering problem largely solved or rapidly being solved in safety-critical verticals, and that the claim overgeneralizes from specific failure cases to a universal architectural indictment that does not hold for well-engineered production systems.
